  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing and strengthening tuberculosis services in key populations across Guyana - Guyana (01-Apr-2019-31-Dec-2021)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Guyana, Tuberculosis, Ministry of Health of the Co-operative Republic of Guyana (MOH)This program has the following goals: Reduce TB related mortality to 7 per 100,000 by 2021.  Reduce TB incidence to 55 per 100,000 by 2021.  Improvecase detection of RR-TB/MDR-TB to at least 85% by 2021.  Reduce TB/HIV related mortality to 3 per 100,000 by 2021. The objectives of this program are: Increase case detection of TB all forms to over 90% by 2021.  Increase case detection of RR-TB/MDR-TB to over 85% by 2021.  Increase TB treatment success for TB all forms to over 90% by 2021.  Increase TB treatment success for RR-TB/MDR-TB to over 85% by 2021.  Increase ART coverage among TB/HIV patients to 100% by 2021.  Increase IPT among newly enrolled PLHIV with TB to over 30% by 2021</narrative>
  </description>
